    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In 2018, Richard Watson tied 200 special "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "transmitters",
            "zh": "信号发射机"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to his cows’ necks. These devices are part of an artificial-intelligence (AI) system named Ida. The system sends messages to Watson’s phone regularly. The messages tell him when his cows are eating and when they are feeling sick. “There may be ten sick animals out there,” said the dairy farmer, “but can you pick them out?”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "AI technologies are reinventing how people work. AI systems read and respond to mountains of information. They are designed to save people time and stress. The Ida system has "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "aroused",
            "ref": "v-arouse"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the interest of many dairy farmers. Watson is one of them. Standing one March morning among his cows, he pulled out his smartphone to show off his Ida app. It showed that Cow #97800 and #97782 were eating less. This might mean that they are feeling ill. Information like this, Watson added, could mean the difference between a cow’s healthy milking and early death. This could save him, and many farmers like him, hundreds of thousands of dollars each year."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Ida was developed by the tech company Connecterra. Yasir Khokhar, the company’s "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "founder",
            "ref": "v-founder"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", said he came up with the idea while living on a Dutch dairy farm. The system was trained to understand cow behaviour by studying thousands of hours of video. It now tracks seven cow behaviours: walking, standing, lying down, eating, "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "chewing",
            "ref": "v-chew"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", drinking, and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "idling",
            "ref": "v-idle"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "However, some farmers say they aren’t that impressed. “I can spot a cow that isn’t feeling great just by looking in her eyes,” said Mark Rodgers, a neighbour of Watson’s. “I can’t draw, paint, or anything else, but I can watch cows.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
